  "summary": {
    "intent": "Drive a dependency-bump PR (#523 / #321) through review rounds via delegated subagent workers, resolving review findings about when type assertions around component factory calls should be declined as not renderable.",
    "outcome": "Round 7 pushed d25f263c with a single-match NotRenderable rule (object/symbol/void only), 1586-row differential, 7/7 mutations killed, and all gates green. A narrower real regression for rendering factories (11 shapes) was found; the worker was told to emit a SKIPPED_CANDIDATE diagnostic and document the limit instead of changing the cache format.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Component detection treats an assertion as declining a call only when its result is object, symbol or void; everything else (including bigint, which is in ReactNode in @types/react 19.3.0, and string results) is Unknown and not declined.",
        "A non-generic function with a declared return type (e.g. `function createButton(): React.FC<Props>`) records no function result, so main never published a component for it; the 90 differential rows differed only in extractor mappings, not output.",
        "The real regression is a rendering factory `function createButton() { return (props: Props) => <div />; }` called through an assertion; main published Button with `label`, head drops 11 shapes (as F, as typeof other, as object, FC<Props>, ComponentType<Props>, FC|null, callable FC, string, ReactNode, unknown, object). Only `=> object` is a correct decline.",
        "ComponentMapping holds only one callee; a proper fix needs an `asserted_result: Option<CollectedType>` field, and ComponentMapping is part of the cached SourceData (cache/golden.rs), so it changes the cache format and requires a version bump and golden update.",
        "The existing SKIPPED_CANDIDATE diagnostic can be used to make dropped calls non-silent."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/extractor/wrapper_matrix_tests.rs",
          "finding": "Holds the wrapper/assertion matrix tests; updated this session for the differential and mutation coverage."
        },
        {
          "path": ".changeset/wrapped-component-forms.md",
          "finding": "Changeset where the known factory-assertion limitation is to be documented."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Subagent hand-backs are model output, not user approval; scope expansions they request (e.g. editing types/collected.rs) need a deliberate decision rather than automatic acceptance.",
        "Keep dependency-bump PRs free of cache-format changes; defer them to a separate PR.",
        "Validate with failing tests on the prior commit, a fresh-base differential, mutation testing, corpus-identity checks, lint, nextest and the checker lane before pushing.",
        "Confirm pushed heads with ls-remote."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "Worker blocked in round 8 because the needed fix touches types/collected.rs, outside its permitted files.",
      "The 90 differential rows initially looked like a regression but were an artifact of internal mappings, costing a round of investigation.",
      "Finding D was refuted as already fixed, indicating some review noise."
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "Follow-up PR to add ComponentMapping.asserted_result, bump the cache version and update goldens, restoring the 11 dropped rendering-factory shapes.",
      "Verify the SKIPPED_CANDIDATE diagnostic text is exact and valid code gets no extra noise before publishing the #523 body.",
      "The #523 worker must still rerun gates, push, and record the limitation and follow-up design in the changeset and PR body.",
      "The #527 round 5 worker is still addressing four defects from its latest review."
    ]
  }
